<title>BELGIUM: AXA BELGIUM HAS 1.3 BLN BFR 1996 PROFIT.</title>
<headline>AXA BELGIUM HAS 1.3 BLN BFR 1996 PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   1.349	vs    0.491</p>
<p>    Premium income	    19.778	vs   15.825</p>
<p>    Technical provisions    16.297	vs   13.727</p>
<p>    Financial income	   4.913	vs    3.853</p>
<p>    Operating costs	    6.158	vs    6.122</p>
<p>NOTE - AXA Belgium SA, Belgium's sixth-largest insurance company, is the main unit in Belgium of France's AXA , which is in the process of a merger with insurer UAP.</p>
<p>AXA Belgium said in a statement that full-year earnings were not comparable with those for 1995 due to the merger with Victoire Belgium SA on July 1, 1995.</p>
<p>AXA Belgium, of which about 5.2 percent is quoted on the Brussels bourse, is part of the AXA Group in Belgium, which also comprises De Kortrijkse Verzekering, Juris and La Mutuelle Patronale.</p>
<p>The Group had a total 1996 turnover of 21.464 billion francs against 20.963 billion a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
